AUDIO: 'upcoming updates here really soon in the video. Cuz first we got to talk about a field that you might have noticed in between our slide sliders and the lore book. This here is our custom rag system. Uh it\'s called rag tag, and it'

[10:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is a user-controlled retrieval augmented generation system with multiple fallback layers built into it. If you\'ve never used a system like this before, it just means you\'re able to have the bot pull'

[10:21] [scene:UI]
VISUAL: Code snippets defining character tags and relations (e.g., "selah", "reinhard") are shown, illustrating the Ragtag system.
AUDIO: 'information when it\'s relevant without destroying the context window by feeding it giant text blobs for every response. You could just write one plain text entry per line, and the system will handle it fine. Or you could take some'

[10:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more control. Rag tag lets you dictate triggers by attaching tags to them and then giving you the ability to weigh those [music] tags. This makes it so that a character who is, let\'s say, an'

[10:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'angel can get pulled with a word like angel, but something like halo and gentle together might also pull the same entry if those combined weights are high'

[11:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'enough. Outside of character cards, custom customization doesn\'t have to stop here. There\'s user-side character cards so that the bot never forgets stuff about who you are. There are scheduled tasks for those who are new to the agent game and just want to dip'

[11:14] [scene:UI]
VISUAL: The "Custom Macros" section is displayed, allowing users to define shortcuts and expansion text.
AUDIO: 'their toes in. And there\'s macros because sometimes you just have some set prompts that you want to send, and you want to be able to do that with like a a single word or string, which is just way easier at the end of the day if you\'re'

[11:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like distracted with something. And the cherry on top of this is the mods tab, where you can throw in some JavaScript or a style sheet to completely change how Gabo Net looks and functions. There\'s pretty much nothing you can\'t do'

